eir current  uh rates of growth and demand and the  underlying all that is a sense that we  have that there is a kind of win-win  here there's opportunity  from the leveling up agenda to have a  stronger economy  overall it is a private sector focused  agenda because we know that  without growing the private sector it  will fundamentally fail you won't  strengthen the places that we are trying  to strengthen for the long term  but there is an opportunity to make the  economy overall we think stronger  because if you have an economy as we've  had for many years where you have parts  of  the country overheating where you can't  get on the train in the morning because  it's so congested where the house prices  are already sky high  and yet at the same time you have other  parts of the country that are crying out  for investment and have space they have  underused assets they have a slack and  labor market then you can see that there  is the potential for a win-win i think  it's no accident that countries that are  more overall balanced economies in the  uk have performed more stronger have  higher living standards higher incomes  and higher gdp so that is what we are  fundamentally in the business of uh of  doing i think it's an incredibly  exciting agenda this morning's  conference has uh talked about some of  the ways that people can get involved in  that agenda and so i think it's been a  really valuable contribution and thank  you for for hosting it i hope it's given  people a bit of a strength of the sense  of the breadth of the agenda here  is not just an economic agenda although  it's centrally an economic agenda it's  also bringing in all those questions  about poor health which can  dog an area's economy as well as  reducing its living standards  bringing in those considerations about  quality of life and the way that places  feel and the opportunities that people  have not just how their economy is  performing so it is an exciting agenda  it's an agenda that is is broad  and i hope that people who have been  involved in your conference this morning  will think about how they can get  involved in it how they can be part of  it through their businesses too and how  we can work together with you to try and  make a big difference for this country  and achieve the potential of a lot of  places that have so much more to give  thank you so much fraser  neil o'brien thanks very much indeed and  that brings us to the end of today's  conference um i hope you've enjoyed  watching thank you for your questions i  hope we went some way to  answering them if you've got any more  than do email us and info spectator dot  co dot uk  we'd like to thank bae systems for  making today possible and i'd also like  to thank cindy you and her production  team for putting this show together stay  tuned to spectator tv's youtube channel  for with a week in 60 minutes and other  shows as we do our best to make sense  with politics as it happens
 

